# ============================================================================
# LEAF-SWAB eDNA | NINE VERTEBRATE ECOLOGICAL TRAIT GLMMs | COMPLETE SCRIPT
# ============================================================================
# PURPOSE: Run nine vertebrate trait models (diet, body size, locomotion)
# using combined binary 12S + 16S detections.
# Unit of analysis: taxon x leaf-swab sample; 288 biological swabs expected.
# Model: Detection ~ Height * Group + Location +
#                    (1|Taxon) + (1|PlotID) + (1|SampleID)
# Family: binomial (logit), fitted with glmmTMB.
# IMPORTANT: Trait category is a taxon-level characteristic. Each taxon belongs
# to ONE group per trait, so Taxon random intercept accounts for repeated taxa.
# Location is a site effect, NOT a replicated forest-condition treatment.
# Outputs: model comparison tables, emmeans, figures, diagnostics, RDS files.
# ============================================================================

